# MCP and API rules

- `designproof_capture`, `designproof_diagnose`, `designproof_redesign`, `designproof_apply`, matrix/proof/design/voice/install_info are the public Cursor surface.
- Tool names are gated by `@designproof/schema` `MCP_TOOL_NAMES` — keep skill docs and `REGISTERED_MCP_TOOLS` in sync.
- `designproof_apply` returns patch text and instructions only. It must never write to the user's repo.
- Web `/api/diagnose` may use deterministic subprocess output; MCP `designproof_diagnose` may add taste when keys exist.
- `GET /api/install-info` and `designproof mcp install cursor` are the Connect Agent source of truth.
- When `DP_CAPTURE_API_TOKEN` is set, diagnose requires Bearer / `x-dp-capture-token`.
- All API failures should return plain-language state and preserve the offline report fallback.
- `/api/setup/*` and `repo-runner.ts` execute cloned repo scripts and are local-dev only.
- Keep `.cursor/mcp.json` registered as `pnpm -F @designproof/mcp start` unless the package script changes.
